1. Definitions

"Askable" means the Askable entity that provides this repository and enters into
the Askable participant agreement.

"Authorized Participant" means an individual who has an active, signed Askable
participant agreement.

"Materials" means this repository and all files, documentation, templates, and
examples contained in it.

"Task Contribution" means any task, code, fixture, verifier, oracle solution,
documentation, or other material created from or submitted with the Materials.

2. Conditional license grant

Subject to continued compliance with this license and an active Askable participant
agreement, Askable grants each Authorized Participant a limited, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable license to copy and use the
Materials solely to create and submit Task Contributions for Askable.

3. Restrictions

Except as expressly permitted in Section 2, you may not:

- use the Materials or Task Contributions for yourself or any third party;
- create, train, evaluate, improve, or distribute a dataset, benchmark, model, or
  product using the Materials or Task Contributions for any party other than
  Askable;
- publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, lease, or otherwise make the Materials
  or Task Contributions available to another person;
- remove proprietary notices or use Askable's name or marks without permission;
- submit an AI-generated task instruction, or use AI tools on a Task
  Contribution without disclosing them and personally verifying every file,
  as required by CONTRIBUTING.md.

4. Task Contributions

Each Task Contribution is subject to the contributor's signed Askable participant
agreement and completed contribution attestation. By submitting a Task
Contribution, the contributor represents that they own, or have sufficient
authority to assign, all rights necessary for Askable's intended use, including
AI-model training, and assigns to Askable all right, title, and interest in that
Task Contribution to the extent permitted by applicable law.

5. No open-source grant

The Materials are not licensed under an open-source license. No rights are granted
to persons who are not Authorized Participants.

6. Termination

The license ends automatically if the participant agreement ends or if the
Authorized Participant breaches this license. On termination, the Authorized
Participant must stop using the Materials and, on Askable's request, delete them
and any Task Contributions not already transferred to Askable.

